Chronological Life Account — Reference Document
Compiled from facts as provided, for use in drafting the memoir. Organized by period, not mythologized.
Origins & Family Background
* Born September 2, 1989, in Portland, Oregon.
* Parents conceived him in Utah before relocating to Oregon; his mother's sister had already moved to the Oregon area, which influenced the family's move.
* Parents met in Utah — father was attending BYU (did not graduate); mother, a Chilean immigrant, had moved from Rexburg to Provo.
* Has an older brother, born before him.
* Father grew up in Minnesota and Nebraska; described by him as reserved, prone to silence/stonewalling.
* Mother described by him as very innocent, childlike.
* Delivered vaginally; the delivering physician was of Indian background.
Early Childhood
* An early, contested memory: recalls a scene of conflict between his parents in which his mother jumped from a ledge and broke her leg; both parents have told him he wasn't present for it, though he remembers it vividly.
* Around age 3–4, his mother met the man who became his stepfather — a former high-level hockey goalie who narrowly missed the 1980 Olympics due to injury, later a successful home-building contractor in the Portland metro area.
* Family lived at "First Place" in Hillsboro, Oregon; house was later remodeled (he went from sharing a room with his brother to having his own).
* Had a young cousin, Matt, as a close friend during this period; no longer in contact.
* Experienced significant childhood sleep anxiety/nightmares; would feign sleep in the car to avoid the bedtime routine.
* Began playing soccer young, coached by his stepfather (teams included "Fire Ants," "Purple People [Leaders]," and later "Team Ice").
* At age five, had a sexual experience with another child, which he describes as having significantly and prematurely shaped his psychological development.
* Younger brother born when he was six.
* Family lived in Hillsboro until third grade, then moved (to Browns Drive); attended Peter Boscow Elementary, then Farmington View Elementary after the move.
Adolescence
* Around age 13, began regularly attending church with his father (not required by his mother/stepfather); his older brother did not attend.
* Stopped competitive soccer around age 13–14.
* Met a friend ("Will") at Farmington View Elementary; by 7th grade (at JB Thomas) they had formed a band together, playing locally until he left for his mission in 2008.
* His friend group in this period used marijuana regularly; he did not use drugs at the time.
* Had unacted-on crushes on girls throughout elementary, middle, and high school.
* Grades declined across high school (A's as a freshman, gradually disengaging by senior year).
Mission & Early Adulthood (2008–2015)
* 2008: Left on a religious mission to Sonora, Mexico (around age 19); baptized several people, including a trucker named Jesus.
* Had been accepted to BYU before the mission.
* Attended BYU after the mission; became disillusioned with the institution/community there.
* Married in his early-to-mid twenties.
* Divorced around age 24 (~2013); has had no contact with his ex-wife since a failed attempt to reach out roughly six months to a year afterward. (Understands she has since remarried.)
* After the divorce: entered a depression, began using drugs and alcohol (primarily marijuana), attempted to finish college but did not complete it.
* June 2015: Moved back in with his parents.
* October 2015: Traveled to Long Island, New York, following an ambulance transport; during this hospital encounter, he discussed a childhood experience from age five, received validation from staff, and was quietly assigned a psychiatric diagnosis in the medical records without a direct in-person confrontation.
Instability & Homelessness (2018–2024)
* 2018: Worked briefly at McDonald's and a pizza place; served roughly 10 days in Washington County (Dallas, OR) jail on charges of petty theft and resisting arrest.
* 2019: Homeless for about 3 months in Hood River, Oregon; then worked Jan–Nov at Royal Moore (Toyota/Mazda/GMC) certified pre-owned car dealership, during which he was housed.
* Lived for a period with a roommate ("Will Mullins," who later legally changed his name to "Douglas"); relationship soured, moved out. Also lived briefly with a roommate named Mario; lost that housing after conflict.
* January 2020: Moved to Arizona to be near his grandmother; homeless for about a month, including periods of eating out of garbage cans.
* While in Arizona, contacted a mental health resource; the organization's owner happened to share his name (Justin David [Lee Harvey]); this person helped stabilize his situation for 2–3 months during the early COVID period.
* Worked as a janitor at Barnes & Noble in Arizona (2020).
* Lived in a backyard RV/unit at a property owned by "Kevin Crosby" (girlfriend "Leslie"); after conflict over unauthorized changes he made to the space, gave up the housing.
* Attempted to walk, then bike, to Mormon Lake, AZ; unsuccessful both times; returned to Oregon.
* Briefly tried living with "Douglas" (formerly Will Mullins) again in Oregon; it didn't work out, leading to renewed homelessness.
* Walked from Oregon to Tillamook (living on about $14 of food over 4 days, including one fasting day), then continued a roughly 3-month walking journey south toward California, aiming for Los Angeles.
* Received a ride from a young woman named Shiloh near Honeyman State Park.
* Got as far as Marin County, California (San Rafael / Corte Madera area) before turning back; had an encounter with a man missing his arms along the way.
* Returned to Oregon via a bus ticket purchased by his mother.
* December 2020: Returned to Arizona.
* 2021 (early part of year): Lived in Arizona; worked at McDonald's.
* Became homeless again in Arizona; moved to Steamboat Springs, Colorado, to live with a friend, Enrique Gomez; trained in jiu-jitsu during this period; situation deteriorated (sobriety-related conflict); left as weather turned cold (~September).
* Moved to Utah; homeless in Springville, then walked toward Tooele pushing a wheelbarrow (painted blue, chalk-lettered) containing a cinder block, in reference to a real long-distance wheelbarrow walker; received a partial ride from a stranger.
* In Tooele: stayed at a transient living house with 4–5 other men, connected with social workers (Christy and Nadine), who purchased his bus ticket back to Oregon.
* Returned to Oregon; lived with mother and stepfather on Shadow Lane.
* October 2021: Attended a cousin's wedding.
* February 2022: Living with his mother (on the floor); working at McDonald's.
* Spring 2022: Worked at Old Spaghetti Factory.
* September 2022–January 2023: Worked as a dishwasher/harvest contributor at a butcher shop in Hillsboro.
* Spring 2023: Had LASIK eye surgery (had worn glasses/contacts since third grade); describes it as symbolically significant — a marker of starting over.
* Around this period: his father was incarcerated (on charges involving a minor).
* 2023: After being asked to leave his mother's house, lived for a time in a hut on community property; was arrested for arson and trespassing after being found burning blackberry bushes (arson charge later dropped).
* 2023: Did part-time wall-washing work for pay (~$50) at a property belonging to Andy Karl Soelberg.
* Winter 2023 into 2024: Moved into the backyard of his mother's house again; lived there roughly a year.
Recent Years (2024–Present)
* Fall 2024 (Sept–Oct): Lived with Rob Hinton, a former Scoutmaster.
* Oct/Nov 2024: Moved to the backyard of a property belonging to Andy Silver.
* November 2024–2026: Navigated various psychiatric systems, including community mental health organizations (LifeWorks NW, Sequoia Mental Health, the Hawthorne Walk-In Clinic), with hospitalizations in Oregon and Colorado.
* Fall 2024–2026: Accepted psychiatric oversight, including an intravenous medication protocol and approximately one year of consultations with a clinician named Dr. Richards, while living in a friend's backyard; this choice was influenced in part by housing and social circumstances.
* April 2025: Started working at Dix Hillsboro Hyundai.
* June 2025: Obtained stable housing in his own room; has been housed and employed since 2025.
* 2026: Elected to discontinue psychiatric oversight by declining the renewal of a six-month anti-psychotic medication dose.
* 2026: Authored "The Bill of Intention: The Unified Operating Structure," a personal philosophy/covenant document (7 articles), designed as a formal PDF.
* More recently: Was involved in what he describes as a high-risk romance scam; reports he came through it safely.
Religious/Belief Trajectory
* Raised within a Mormon (LDS) family framework on his father's side, including folk-magic elements from his paternal grandmother; his mother was raised in it but less attached to it. He was drawn to its "signs and tokens" for a long time.
* Over the years, bounced between various belief systems/frameworks (including a period of contact with Falun Dafa, which he does not currently follow).
* Ultimately concluded he does not need an external belief system — this conclusion is what led directly to writing the Bill of Intention: a self-authored operating structure meant to unify daily execution with philosophy and remove the decision fatigue of not having a fixed framework. Notes his father has operated similarly (without a fixed framework) for a long time, which he says he shared until he "branched off."
Additional Record Notes
* Describes past marijuana use as a reaction to existential anxiety.
* Reports stints of alcohol use and marijuana-gummy use during 2025 and into 2026; states he has since stopped using either, by choice rather than framing it as having been a problem per se — says he simply decided they "don't add to my life."
